This info on the connection between the deltoids and trapezius proves that by gaining more anatomical knowledge, I can make my new Marie doll far more accurate.

157
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:09,540
Question for you, Gordon. I thought you said you had trouble spending time in the sun without getting burnt. Were you able to get over that?

158
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:17,020
Yes, I can stay out as long as I'd like to now. It's all thanks to this special sunblock. Would you care to try it out for yourself?

159
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:19,360
I'd love to. Thanks for offering.

160
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:24,240
You need to be meticulous when dealing with UV rays. Here you go.

161
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:28,200
That's cold. Just what do you think you're doing back there?

162
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,700
Huh? What?

163
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:33,740
Hello. Here you go.

164
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:41,100
Who the hell says you can't have beer for breakfast?

165
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,080
Captain, for you.

166
00:06:43,260 --> 00:06:47,020
Thanks. Aren't you going to train like the rest of the squad?

167
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:51,560
Glad we talked.

168
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:58,720
Hey, guys! Food's ready! Come and get it!

169
00:07:08,460 --> 00:07:09,580
Thanks for the meal!

170
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:19,080
It's that song again!

171
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:21,940
Eh? Noel?

172
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:37,460
This is about where I was the first time I heard it.

173
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:38,660
Hey!

174
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:40,420
Asta?

175
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:42,380
Did something happen or what?

176
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:46,200
Not exactly. But do you hear anything strange?

177
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:46,920
Like what?

178
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:59,640
Hey, look!

179
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:00,880
Wait, Kahono?

180
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:02,100
And Kieto!

181
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:04,120
What are you doing here?

182
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:09,080
I could ask the same, but since you're exactly who we're looking for, I'll chalk it up to Providence.

183
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:11,900
The sea goddess is as beautiful as ever.

184
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,660
So what gives? Is there trouble at home?

185
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:17,320
Oh, right. We came to ask for help.

186
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:22,180
It's bad. We ask that you meet us back at the temple.

187
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:27,180
You were attacked by a monster?

188
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:30,360
A strong one? Likely a guardian of the sea.

189
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:35,020
They've been around since time immemorial. They're said to be servants of the sea god.

190
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:40,100
So this creature is sacred? If you served the same god, then why would it attack you?

191
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:44,220
Something's begun to disturb the flow of mana in this part of the sea.

192
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:48,120
As a result, much of the local fauna has become quite aggressive.

193
00:08:49,580 --> 00:08:52,660
I decided to investigate with magic, and then I saw it.

194
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,920
The mana disturbance made it hard to make out details.

195
00:08:55,920 --> 00:09:06,960
But I know what I saw. South of this temple in a place called the Void of No Return, there lurks a guardian of the sea that has been wholly consumed by its own rage.

196
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:12,500
I'm sure that the disturbance I felt in the mana here was caused by this guardian's fury.

197
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:19,260
The temple mages might have calmed the guardian by performing their song and dance, but they never got a chance to try.

198
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:22,800
Our best warriors were wounded trying to defend us.

199
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:24,400
Kahono.

200
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:29,020
Well, we brought you here to request that you grant Kiyoto and Kahono your protection.

201
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:33,640
Please use your considerable strength to escort them to the Void of No Return safely.

202
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:38,600
Sounds like a whole lot of not my problem. We're all really busy training right now.

203
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:40,920
You spent all day drinking in a beach chair!

204
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:45,280
Please, sir. I ask because I know how powerful the Black Bulls are.

205
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:52,940
You proved this in the Battle Royale we fought, and through your ability to reach the underwater temple safely, despite being land dwellers.

206
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:56,140
Though that was through the Sea Goddess's protection.

207
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:06,000
This may sound harsh, but have you got any proof that your song and dance can actually calm this guardian down?

208
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:08,280
Not exactly.

209
00:10:08,780 --> 00:10:11,680
Protecting the kingdom isn't a hobby for us. It's a job.

210
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:14,580
We need to put our efforts where we know they'll count.

211
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:18,420
I'm not about to loan you my squad members when your resolve is this week.

212
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:24,040
So basically, we just need to convince you that this could work.

213
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:26,120
Huh? What do you mean?

214
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:29,660
This mana disturbance is affecting a massive part of the sea.

215
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:32,280
It's possible that there's a devil behind this, too.

216
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:34,960
As magic knights, we are sworn to protect.

217
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:38,760
I'll get your mages to the Guardian safely. There's no doubt in my mind.

218
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:39,660
Noelle.

219
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,380
The Sea Goddess provides.

220
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:48,220
I'm sure now, we'll quell the Guardian's rage. You have my word.

221
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:52,280
We've sung and danced for the Almighty Sea God. We're prepared for this task.

222
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:55,940
One way or another, we will make the Guardian hear our prayers.

223
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:59,020
That's the kind of resolve I can get behind.

224
00:10:59,020 --> 00:11:01,900
Now, convince me it'll work.

225
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:05,800
I have a plan. And I think you'll like it.

226
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:17,780
It's over there. See it?

227
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:20,620
The Void of No Return.

228
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:25,700
Its name is based on the legend that those who wander into its depths are never seen again.

229
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:31,740
We were told stories as kids, but I never thought they were real.

230
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:34,880
Even now, it's a bit of a struggle to believe my eyes.

231
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:37,280
How deep do you think this goes?

232
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:44,260
So, what's your plan?

233
00:11:45,060 --> 00:11:48,540
I'll make a smaller and more powerful version of the Sea Dragon's Cradle.

234
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,620
There's a trade-off. It'll be durable, but it won't carry more than four people.

235
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:57,360
Well, with you, Kahano, and Kyoto, we've already got our first three passengers.

236
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,500
Well, we could still fit one more...

237
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:00,760
Me! Me! Me!

238
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:03,020
Please, oh man, I want to go so bad!

239
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,480
Why sing to the Guardian when we could kill it?

240
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:08,120
I wonder how strong it is. I can't wait to find out!

241
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:10,020
Just send me and I'll get it done quickly.

242
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:12,760
Marie awaits me. Her deltoids need carving.

243
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:14,780
Please tell me there's something I'm missing here!

244
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,700
Maybe this Guardian wants to rejoin the cycle of life!

245
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:19,680
Talk about well-aged meat, am I right?

246
00:12:20,060 --> 00:12:21,800
Yeah, I'm not sending any of you.

247
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:22,520
What?

248
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:25,700
And you're not going either.

249
00:12:27,020 --> 00:12:29,140
Are you serious, sir? Why?

250
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:30,920
Is it because I can't swim?

251
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:33,520
Forgot about that. You really can't go.

252
00:12:34,660 --> 00:12:35,960
This isn't fair!

253
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:37,340
He's such an idiot.

254
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:41,040
Fenril, you go.

255
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:41,700
Huh?

256
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,260
Get him out if things go bad.

257
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:46,360
Even if you have to die to do it.

258
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:47,540
Understood?

259
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:50,280
Yes, sir!

260
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,260
Oh, and Noel.

261
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:57,600
You're the one who decided to do this, so make sure you see it through.

262
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:58,340
Sir!

263
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:04,540
Such violent mana.

264
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:07,760
If I let my guard down for even a second, we're finished.

265
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:10,280
Look there!

